description:
In packages/swf/src/compile.ts around line 1112-1119, the call to encodeDefineMorphShape2() always passes null, null for startHints/endHints:

    const morphBody = encodeDefineMorphShape2(
      morphCharId,
      startObj.shape.paths,
      endObj.shape.paths,
      null,   // startHints — NEVER passed
      null,   // endHints — NEVER passed
      ...
    );

Task 0837 (bf167d9) wired shape hints into interpolateShapeTween (preview) and added hint support to encodeDefineMorphShape2, but did NOT update compile.ts to forward the keyframe's shapeHints. The model stores them on Frame.shapeHints (startKf.shapeHints, endKf.shapeHints), and these are already available at the call site (startKf and endKf are in scope around line 1078-1084). The fix is to pass startKf.shapeHints ?? null and endKf.shapeHints ?? null as the 4th and 5th arguments. This is a one-line fix but must be verified with the morph-hints e2e oracle (morphshape-hints.test.ts is a unit test; a Ruffle-based e2e would be stronger evidence).
